# A Borg cube holds a Klingon destroyer with its Holding Beam. Both ships are set to green alert so nothing fires. The
# destroyer is given a move order, then the cube is selected and F4 is pressed and the destroyer clicked (the special step).
# The cube's special energy falls from its 1000 by the 50 cost and 50 a second less the 10 it regains; the destroyer's
# position and yaw in the dumps stay what they were at the first dump while the beam runs. The beam is turned off before
# its first boarding party, a second after it starts, so the destroyer is not boarded (play/borg-assimilation.play). `special 4` alone turns the beam
# off with no refund, the energy stops falling, and the destroyer drives on.
# Run it with --layout layouts/special-weapon.jsonc; the layout's header comment has the whole command.
# The move point is in the frame of the dump's pos= field, whose z is the layout z mirrored.
wait 0.5
select Victim
press Shift+G
move 2300 -2000
select Cube
press Shift+G
expect Cube special >= 1000
special 4 Victim
wait 0.5
dump held1
expect Cube special < 960
expect Cube special > 900
wait 0.4
dump held2
expect Cube special < 920
special 4
wait 0.1
dump off
expect Cube special > 700
wait 3
dump after
expect Cube special > 700
